#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""agent-resume: resurrect a Claude Code teammate into its swarm tmux session.

Usage: agent-resume [<selector>] [options] [...forwarded to claude]

The leading bare argument is classified by shape:
    2a38de2d-bd34-...   session UUID       -> --resume
    teammate@session-x  full agent id      -> --agent-id
    session-a52cb2af    a dir under teams/ -> --team (whole roster, lead last)
    teammate            bare agent name    -> resolved, or refused if several rosters claim it

--to-team TEAM|live rebinds a member onto another team: it relaunches the agent
with that team's identity, replaces whichever process still holds the
transcript, registers it in the destination roster and retires the source entry.

--install sets up the ~/.local/bin symlink and zsh tab completion.

Or select explicitly with --agent-id (as claude spells it) and/or --resume <session-uuid>.
Everything the harness needs to relaunch it (team, type, color, model, effort,
permission mode, cwd, parent session, tmux socket + pane) is reconstructed from
three on-disk sources plus the live process table; when they disagree, the most
recent value wins.

Any flag agent-resume does not recognise is forwarded verbatim to claude, and a
forwarded flag overrides the value agent-resume would have derived.
"""

